            "notes": "In round 2, start to build up your healing output.\n\nGain weapon damage and attack speed with [Advanced Nanobiotics](item_26fcf7c9-b81a-4d8e-a459-b515519cb73e) and [Custom Stock](item_17d633af-8bcc-4893-b865-be0a7bc66fe2) which boosts the healing provided by [Enlightenment](item_8392e752-ca6b-487d-9580-11eab6075c3c). The additional ability power will also increase the healing output of OH regardless if you're dealing damage.\n\nSell [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) to afford the two rare items.\n\nRound 2 affects:\n* Orb of Harmony (OH):\n- Healing increased from 30 hp/sec to 33 hp/sec.\n* Orb of Destruction (OD):\n- Damage increased from 50 to 55.\n- Replenishes 5 hp per hit.\n- Boosts OH healing by 19 hp per hit.\n- After healing, attack speed increased from 0.4 seconds to 0.36 for three seconds.\n- After elimination, attack speed increased from 0.4 seconds to 0.33 seconds for three seconds.\n= Max attack speed possible: 0.3 seconds for three seconds while healing and after an elimination.\n* Snap Kick (SK):\n- Damage increased from 60 to 66.\n- Replenishes 6 hp with each hit.\n- Boosts OH healing by 23 hp per hit.\n\nIf survivability is a problem, pick up [Reinforced Titanium](item_8ebaa7db-aedf-48ed-adc1-318cb46a3214) instead of [Advanced Nanobiotics](item_26fcf7c9-b81a-4d8e-a459-b515519cb73e).\n\nAlso, if your Juno or Mercy support is struggling to survive, you can take [Breezeborne Blessing](item_90dbbc8e-b405-40a9-9564-8fa3a35a0202) to help keep them alive since they are likely the team's primary healing source.",
