            "notes": "If you have reached round 5, the other team has won at least a round or two meaning wins aren\u2019t yet guaranteed. So this round, pick the power that addresses the greater team weakness. If your DPS or tank are flanking a lot or diving beyond view, take  [Gotta Have Faith](item_b1c30cfc-b920-4d1e-91f3-98c16ca0c3d7). If you are being targeted a lot, take [Inner Peace](item_3cb26943-7c02-4aa2-97d0-7411dac1073c) to increase survivability.\n\nFor items, take [Teacher's Totem](item_32e3e66c-1fc1-46d0-b3fb-6438a4583c26). This will increase your survivability by boosting your shields as well as reducing the damage your OH\u2019d teammates (and yourself if you took Inner Peace) receive from abilities. If you\u2019d rather focus on healing instead of damage reduction, you can take [Friendship Bracelet](item_abc52eaf-cb2e-4e0b-8b5d-15e9f7bae003) to boost the power of OH by up to 30% (though this requires leaving the backline to get into the thick of the fight without any increased survivability.)\n\nRound 5 effects:\n* Orb of Harmony (OH):\n- Healing decreased from 30 hp/sec to 25 hp/sec.\n- Reduces ability damage received by 10%.\n* Orb of Destruction (OD):\n- Damage increased from 50 to 67.\n- Replenishes 6 hp per hit.\n- Boosts OH healing by 23 hp per hit.\n- Attack speed increased from 0.4 seconds to 0.36.\n- After healing, attack speed increased from 0.36 seconds to 0.32 seconds for three seconds.\n* Snap Kick (SK):\n- Damage increased from 60 to 81.\n- Replenishes 8 hp with each hit.\n- Boosts OH healing by 28 hp per hit.\n\nIf you couldn\u2019t afford Genji\u2019s Galvanic Gloves in Round 4, sell the rare items you bought to pick it up this round. If after this you can\u2019t afford Teacher\u2019s Totem, supplement with these rare items: Wrist Wraps (increase base OH healing and utilization of Enlightenment), Breezeborne Blessing (increase base OH healing), Emergency Chip (increase weapon power and survivability).",
